answer.text:
Assuming both PMOS devices are in saturation, the bias gates and \(V_{DD}\) are small-signal grounds. Thus \(M_2\) has \(v_{gs2}=0\), so it contributes only \(r_{o2}\) from node \(X\) to ac ground. Node \(X\) is therefore the source degeneration node for \(M_1\).

Using a test voltage \(v_t\) at the output,

\[
v_X=i_t r_{o2}
\]

and for \(M_1\),

\[
i_t=\frac{v_t-v_X}{r_{o1}}-(g_{m1}+g_{mb1})v_X .
\]

Solving,

\[
\boxed{
R_{out}=r_{o1}+r_{o2}+(g_{m1}+g_{mb1})r_{o1}r_{o2}
}
\]

If body effect is neglected,

\[
\boxed{
R_{out}=r_{o1}+r_{o2}+g_{m1}r_{o1}r_{o2}
\approx g_{m1}r_{o1}r_{o2}
}
\]

Note the boosting term uses \(g_{m1}\), because \(M_1\) is the cascode device whose drain is the output node.

With \(V_{DD}\), \(V_{b1}\), and \(V_{b2}\) as small-signal grounds, node \(X\) sees resistance \(r_{o2}\) through \(M_2\). Thus \(M_1\) is source-degenerated by \(r_{o2}\), so

\[
\boxed{
R_{\text{out}}
=
r_{o1}+\left[1+(g_{m1}+g_{mb1})r_{o1}\right]r_{o2}
}
\]

equivalently,

\[
\boxed{
R_{\text{out}}
=
r_{o1}+r_{o2}+(g_{m1}+g_{mb1})r_{o1}r_{o2}
\approx
(g_{m1}+g_{mb1})r_{o1}r_{o2}
}
\]

If body effect is neglected, set \(g_{mb1}=0\):

\[
R_{\text{out}}\approx g_{m1}r_{o1}r_{o2}.
\]

Assume low frequency, negligible gate current, and neglect channel-length modulation/body effect. \(V_{DD}\) and \(V_b\) are ac grounds and \(I_{SS}\) only sets bias.

Node \(X\):

\[
v_X=-g_{m1}R_{D1}v_P .
\]

For the source-coupled pair \(M_2,M_3\), with the gate of \(M_3\) at ac ground,

\[
(g_{m2}+g_{m3})v_S=g_{m2}v_X,
\qquad
i_o=g_{m3}v_S
\]

so

\[
i_o=\frac{g_{m2}g_{m3}}{g_{m2}+g_{m3}}v_X .
\]

Thus the open-circuit voltage gain from \(P\) to \(V_{out}\) is

\[
A_v=\frac{v_{out}}{v_P}
=
-g_{m1}R_{D1}
\left(\frac{g_{m2}g_{m3}}{g_{m2}+g_{m3}}\right)R_{D2}
\equiv -A_0 .
\]

The feedback resistor is reflected to the input as

\[
Z_F=\frac{R_F+R_{D2}}{1-A_v}
=
\frac{R_F+R_{D2}}{1+A_0}.
\]

Therefore the impedance seen by \(I_{in}\) at node \(P\) is

\[
\boxed{
Z_{in}(s)=
\left[
\frac{1}{R_{in}}
+sC_{in}
+
\frac{
1+g_{m1}R_{D1}
\left(\dfrac{g_{m2}g_{m3}}{g_{m2}+g_{m3}}\right)R_{D2}
}{
R_F+R_{D2}
}
\right]^{-1}
}
\]

Equivalently, \(Z_{in}(s)=R_{eq}/(1+sR_{eq}C_{in})\), where \(R_{eq}\) is the parallel combination above.

If \(R_F\gg R_{D2}\), this reduces to the usual Miller approximation

\[
Z_{in}(s)\approx
\left[
\frac{1}{R_{in}}+sC_{in}+
\frac{1+A_0}{R_F}
\right]^{-1}.
\]
